CHAPTER.VERS:
How long, you

          {+}
         simple ones, will you

          {+}
         love simplicity? And scoffers delight themselves in scoffing, And fools hate knowledge?

Turn

          {+}
         at my reproof: Look, I will cause my spirit to gush out on you

          {+}
         I will make my words known to you

          {+}
        .

Because I have called, and you

          {+}
         have refused; I have stretched out my hand, and no man has regarded;

But you

          {+}
         have set at nothing all my counsel, And would have none of my reproof:

I also will laugh in [the day of] your

          {+}
         calamity; I will mock when your

          {+}
         fear comes;

When your

          {+}
         fear comes as a storm, And your

          {+}
         calamity comes on as a whirlwind; When distress and anguish come upon you

          {+}
        .
